IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pid-rules`
IMPORT `pid-dates`
IMPORT `pid-seat`

-- Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (Cth) -- cases for the discloser's questions (pid-seat.l4).
-- Every expected value is worked by hand from the deposited text (Compilation No. 20), with the section, and never copied
-- from the encoding's output. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the discloser`

§§ `s 26(1)(a), s 69, s 70 -- public official`

-- s 69(1) table items: in; s 69(1) is a 'means' definition, so outside it no; s 70 deems; s 69(4) and s 70(3A) exclude.
#ASSERT `Am I a public official who can make a public interest disclosure?` `an APS employee in a Department` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official who can make a public interest disclosure?` `a contracted service provider for a Commonwealth contract or its officer or employee providing services for the contract` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official who can make a public interest disclosure?` `a member of the Defence Force or a cadet or officer or instructor in the Australian Defence Force Cadets` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official who can make a public interest disclosure?` `the Registrar or a Deputy Registrar of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Corporations` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official who can make a public interest disclosure?` `none of these` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official who can make a public interest disclosure?` `none of these` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official who can make a public interest disclosure?` `a judicial officer` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official who can make a public interest disclosure?` `a member of Parliament` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official who can make a public interest disclosure?` `a person employed under the Members of Parliament (Staff) Act 1984` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official who can make a public interest disclosure?` `a member of a Royal Commission` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `ss 29-33 -- disclosable conduct`

-- s 29(1): a table kind by (a) an agency, (b) an official in connection with the position, (c) a contractor for the contract.
-- s 29(2)(b) reaches an official's conduct outside the position; (2)(a), (b) do not reach an agency; s 29(2A) personal
-- work-related conduct is out unless a reprisal or significant; ss 31, 32, 33 exclude.
-- Flags after the kind: personal work-related, reprisal, significant, policy only, court or tribunal, intelligence agency.
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `an agency` `conduct that contravenes a law of the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `a public official in connection with their position` `conduct that contravenes a law of the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `a contracted service provider in connection with entering into or giving effect to the Commonwealth contract` `conduct that results in the wastage of relevant money or property or of the money or property of a prescribed authority` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `an agency` `conduct of a kind prescribed by the PID rules` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `someone else` `conduct that contravenes a law of the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `a public official not in connection with their position` `conduct that contravenes a law of the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `an agency` `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `a public official not in connection with their position` `conduct of a public official that could if proved give reasonable grounds for disciplinary action ending their engagement or appointment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `a public official in connection with their position` `a public official abusing their position as a public official` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `an agency` `a public official abusing their position as a public official` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `a public official in connection with their position` `conduct that contravenes a law of the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `a public official in connection with their position` `conduct that contravenes a law of the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `a public official in connection with their position` `conduct that contravenes a law of the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `a public official in connection with their position` `conduct that contravenes a law of the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `an agency` `conduct that contravenes a law of the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `a public official in connection with their position` `conduct that contravenes a law of the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `an agency` `conduct that contravenes a law of the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

