§§ `s 20 -- identity`

-- Order: I made a PID, what they did, obtained as a public official, likely to identify me, exception.
#ASSERT `Would revealing or using information that identifies me be an offence?` TRUE `disclosed it to someone other than me` TRUE TRUE `no exception` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Would revealing or using information that identifies me be an offence?` TRUE `disclosed it only to me` TRUE TRUE `no exception` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Would revealing or using information that identifies me be an offence?` TRUE `used it` TRUE TRUE `no exception` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Would revealing or using information that identifies me be an offence?` TRUE `disclosed it to someone other than me` TRUE TRUE `I consented or acted inconsistently with keeping my identity confidential` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Would revealing or using information that identifies me be an offence?` TRUE `disclosed it to someone other than me` TRUE TRUE `the information had already been lawfully published` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Would revealing or using information that identifies me be an offence?` TRUE `disclosed it to someone other than me` TRUE TRUE `for the purposes of this Act such as assisting with the disclosure or giving legal advice about it or performing a function under the Act` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Would revealing or using information that identifies me be an offence?` TRUE `used it` TRUE TRUE `for the purposes of a Commonwealth law or a prescribed State or Territory law` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Would revealing or using information that identifies me be an offence?` FALSE `disclosed it to someone other than me` TRUE TRUE `no exception` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Would revealing or using information that identifies me be an offence?` TRUE `disclosed it to someone other than me` FALSE TRUE `no exception` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Would revealing or using information that identifies me be an offence?` TRUE `disclosed it to someone other than me` TRUE FALSE `no exception` EQUALS FALSE

§§ `s 43(11), s 52 -- timing`

-- 'within N days after' day D: the last day is D + N (fork F1); no weekend roll (fork F2).
#ASSERT `By when should my disclosure be allocated?` (`the day` 3 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 17 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when should my disclosure be allocated?` (`the day` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `the day` 3 1 2027
-- 31 Jan 2026 + 90: to 28 Feb is 28, to 31 Mar 59, to 30 Apr 89, so 1 May 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the investigation be completed?` (`the day` 31 1 2026) 0 EQUALS `the day` 1 5 2026
#ASSERT `By when must the investigation be completed?` (`the day` 31 1 2026) 30 EQUALS `the day` 31 5 2026
-- 1 Dec 2027 + 90: to 31 Dec is 30, to 31 Jan 61, to 29 Feb 2028 (a leap year) 90.
